icit GEMM)  + GELU, written directly into the linear\n      A-matrix layout [B, T3, 3840] with column k = c*10 + f (fused reshape)\n  K-D linear (GEMM) + scale + positional-embedding add -> out bf16 [B, T3, 1024]\n\nAll conv/linear accumulation is fp32; intermediates are rounded to bf16 at the\nsame sites as the reference (round conv output to bf16 -> GELU in fp32 ->\nround to bf16). GELU is exact-erf (matches F.gelu default).\n\nPyTorch is used only for tensor metadata / buffer allocation / launch plumbing.\n\"\"\"","new_string":"\"\"\"\nKDA candidate c006 — L2/015 Audio Sinusoidal PE + Conv Projection.\n\nDIAGNOSTIC candidate (fully Triton; NOT a compute fallback — it deliberately\nreturns zeros and will report INCORRECT, never faking a pass). Its sole purpose\nis to recover observability the evaluator withholds.\n\nLineage / debugging campaign — the real 4-kernel pipeline has NEVER compiled;\nevery candidate returned 0/5 uniform, shape-independent RUNTIME_ERROR with NO\ntraceback exposed by the evaluator (per-workload JSON carries only `status`):\n  c001 (tl.math.erf)              -> 0/5   [erf/libdevice suspect]\n  c002 (inlined polynomial erf)   -> 0/5   erf/libdevice RULED OUT\n  c003 (explicit-2D conv3 col)    -> 0/5   broadcast rank RULED OUT\n  c004 (tl.range->range, stages2) -> 0/5   loop-pipelining RULED OUT\n  c005 (tl.dot 3-arg accumulate)  -> 0/5   dot call convention RULED OUT\n\nFour well-motivated single-surface fixes were all refuted and static inspection\nfound nothing further. With zero traceback, blind edits are low-information.\nPIVOT to BISECTION: this candidate keeps the module intact (all real kernels\nstill DEFINED, so module import behaviour is unchanged; @triton.jit does not\ncompile a kernel until it is launched) but `run()` launches ONLY a trivial\nTriton memset kernel that fills the output with zeros. The real conv/linear\nkernels are defined-but-not-launched, hence not compiled here.\n\nINTERPRETATION of c006's evaluator status:\n  * INCORRECT (numeric mismatch, NOT RUNTIME_ERROR): module import + run()\n    shape/alloc plumbing + a basic Triton JIT launch all work => the compile\n    fault is isolated to the conv/linear kernels. Later candidates reintroduce\n    them one at a time (conv1 only, then +conv2, ...) to pinpoint the first\n    kernel that raises.\n  * RUNTIME_ERROR: the fault is at import / harness / Triton-availability level,\n    independent of the real kernels => redirects the entire diagnosis (e.g. a\n    module-level import, decorator, or run() signature issue).\n\nThe real kernels below (conv1/conv2/conv3/linear) are preserved verbatim from\nc005 so the eventual reintroduction is a pure launch-site change.\n\nPyTorch is used only for tensor metadata / buffer allocation / launch plumbing.\n\"\"\""}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":146749,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c1ac1ce-62a7-45ff-ba86-9406f5f1f62e","uuid":"a78abb8e-9082-47d6-a1c8-621ddd320ab8","timestamp":"2026-09-17T22:17:05.666Z"}
