ast in conv3_to_A_kernel: `col = offs_n * FREQ3 + ho[:, None]` adds a rank-1 [BN] tensor to a rank-2 [BM,1] tensor, which Triton rejects at compile time regardless of shape. Fixing it to `offs_n[None,:]*FREQ3 + ho[:,None]` (explicit [1,BN]+[BM,1]->[BM,BN]) should let the pipeline compile.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"conv3_to_A_kernel column index made an explicit 2D broadcast: `col = offs_n[None, :] * FREQ3 + ho[:, None]`. No other changes.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"single line: explicit 2D broadcast for conv3 output column index.\", \"validation\": {\"structural_guards\": \"pass\", \"all_workloads_pass\": false, \"per_workload\": [{\"wl\": \"w1\", \"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w2\", \"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w3\", \"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w4\", \"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w5\", \"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}]}, \"workloads\": [{\"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": null, \"valid\": false, \"decision\": \"rejected\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 3, \"skills_used\": [], \"skill_usage\": \"KernelWiki: not applicable (Ampere sm_80).\", \"static_checks\": [\"grep-verified explicit 2D broadcasts across all kernels; addressing/stride math re-derived and confirmed correct for NCHW input, NHWC intermediates, and the [N,K] linear weight\"], \"notes\": \"REFUTED: the col rank-mismatch was not the (only) root cause; identical uniform RUNTIME_ERROR persists. Evaluator exposes no traceback (per_workload has only status). Remaining shared, untouched suspects live in conv1_kernel / conv_nhwc_kernel / linear_kernel / run(); addressing math re-verified correct. Strongest remaining hypothesis: the version-fragile pipelined loop construct `tl.range(...)` used in conv2/conv3/linear (the dot-using kernels). conv1 launches first and has NO tl.range, so a tl.range compile failure in conv2 is consistent with an all-workloads RUNTIME_ERROR. Next c004: replace every `tl.range(...)` with canonical Python `range(...)` over constexpr bounds (official Triton matmul tutorial form), keep num_stages conservative.\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c004\", \"candidate\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c003\", \"source_sha256\": \"28fc78e63b6545da03a1310a065503eff7f3825a399b5c70a17762a5a8f92c64\", \"phase\": \"feedback\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T20:01:03Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The uniform RUNTIME_ERROR is a Triton compile error in the dot-using kernels (conv2/conv3/linear). The remaining version-fragile construct is `tl.range(...)` (a pipelined-loop hint). Replacing every `tl.range(0,..,BLOCK_K)` inner k-loop with canonical Python `range(...)` (official matmul tutorial form) and lowering all dot-kernel num_stages to 2 should let it compile.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"conv2/conv3/linear inner k-loops: `tl.range(...)` -> `range(...)`; num_stages 3->2 for all three dot-kernel launches. conv1 and all math/layout/addressing unchanged.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"loop construct (tl.range->range) + num_stages 3->2 on the three dot kernels.\", \"validation\": {\"structural_guards\": \"pass\", \"all_workloads_pass\": false, \"per_workload\": [{\"wl\": \"w1\", \"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w2\", \"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w3\", \"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w4\", \"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}, {\"wl\": \"w5\", \"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"passed\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_ms\": null, \"ref_latency_ms\": null}]}, \"workloads\": [{\"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"dedae7e8-65de-5163-9c0e-4cf292aef154\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"c8362d74-604f-509b-8b18-86ff78b4316f\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"67119fc1-69aa-53a7-acd5-dae7dbbcbd56\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}, {\"uuid\": \"10361f03-c94e-514e-bb4a-6799525e65d5\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\"}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": null, \"valid\": false, \"decision\": \"rejected\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 4, \"skills_used\": [], \"skill_usage\": \"KernelWiki: not applicable (Ampere sm_80).\", \"static_checks\": [\"grep-verified no tl.range remains in kernel bodies; all inner k-loops now plain range(); num_stages=2 on all four launches\"], \"notes\": \"REFUTED: tl.range/num_stages was not the cause; identical uniform RUNTIME_ERROR persists. Cleared surfaces so far: erf/libdevice (c002), broadcast rank (c003), loop-pipelining (c004). Remaining live single-surface suspects: (a) the tl.dot CALL CONVENTION `tl.dot(a,w,out_dtype=tl.float32)` in conv2/conv3/linear -- switch to the canonical 3-arg accumulate form `acc = tl.dot(a,w,acc)` (tutorial-exact, no out_dtype kwarg); (b) conv1_kernel itself (unchanged since c001) or run()-setup asserts. Next c005: switch all three dots to the accumulate form. If still RUNTIME_ERROR, the dot convention is cleared and the following candidate will target conv1/run() directly (e.g., a diagnostic that isolates whether conv1 alone executes).\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c005\", \"candidate\": \"c005\", \"parent\": \"c004\", \"source_sha256\": \"57b1f16f1e80e2bdca7d2dbb5badd647e23b5f1b699006871a09cac8a36ba08a\", \"phase\": \"feedback\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T21:12:24Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The uniform RUNTIME_ERROR is a Triton compile error at the tl.dot call convention. All three dot kernels used `acc += tl.dot(a, w, out_dtype=tl.float32)`; the `out_dtype=` kwarg is version-fragile. Switch every call to the tutorial-exact 3-arg accumulate form `acc = tl.dot(a, w, acc)` (fp32 accumulator carried in positionally, no out_dtype kwarg). Semantically identical fp32 accumulation.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"All three `acc += tl.dot(a, w, out_dtype=tl.float32)` (conv2/conv3/linear) -> `acc = tl.dot(a, w, acc)`. No other changes.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \